# Build context for the api/ image. Default deny, then let four things back in.
#
# Why it is written this way round: the repository is ~1.2 GB (698 MB of .git,
# 215 MB of PDFs, 340 MB of audio) and every byte of the build context is packed
# up and shipped to the builder before the first instruction runs. A deny-list
# would have to name each of those and would silently start shipping the next
# large folder somebody adds. This way the context is a few megabytes and stays
# that way — anything new is excluded until it is named here.
#
# Docker cannot re-include a path whose parent is excluded, which is why site/
# and site/tools/ are re-included and then re-emptied on the way down.
*

!api
!site
site/*
!site/tools
site/tools/*
!site/tools/tiers.py
!site/tools/tiers.json

# Nothing below is needed at runtime, and __pycache__ from a local run would
# otherwise be copied over the interpreter's own bytecode.
api/__pycache__
api/README.md
**/.DS_Store
